  "articleBody": "Knowing when to tackle a painting project yourself and when to call in a pro can save you a lot of hassle. For bathroom painting and trim, there are definite signs it's time to bring in the experts at HH Remodeling LLC: \n\n*   **Persistent peeling or mildew:** If you're constantly fighting peeling paint or mildew, it's often a sign of underlying moisture or ventilation problems that need a professional diagnosis, not just another coat of paint. \n*   **Complex trim work:** If your bathroom has intricate trim profiles, built-ins, or multiple angles, precise cuts and seamless finishes are tough to achieve for a DIYer. Professionals ensure those details look perfect. \n*   **Coordination with other trades:** When painting needs to happen alongside new tile, flooring, or plumbing, a professional can coordinate the sequencing to prevent damage and rework, ensuring everything flows smoothly. \n*   **Uneven walls or extensive repairs:** If your walls need significant patching, sanding, or skim coating to achieve a smooth finish, a professional painter has the tools and expertise to make them look flawless before the first brushstroke. \n*   **Need for specific products and methods:** Pros know exactly which mildew-resistant paints, primers, and caulks are best for wet environments, ensuring long-lasting results and avoiding common failures.",
